WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-FR

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.108
We celebrate a victory for anyone,
left, right, or center,

00:00:03.119 --> 00:00:07.548
struggling with the skyrocketing cost
of living from gas to groceries to housing,

00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:10.833
anyone who's sick of the tariffs,
the endless war,

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.813
the tax breaks for big corporations paid
for by cuts to your health care.

00:00:14.824 --> 00:00:17.273
Anyone who's fed up
with the most corrupt president

00:00:17.284 --> 00:00:20.233
in our history who has failed
in his way of governing.

00:00:20.244 --> 00:00:24.273
And anyone who knows that we can do so much
better if we work together.

00:00:24.284 --> 00:00:27.093
So we know this was a hard-fought
victory tonight.

00:00:27.104 --> 00:00:30.573
It was made even harder by the tens
and tens of millions

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:33.773
of dollars that poured into New
Hampshire from Donald Trump, Elon Musk,

00:00:33.784 --> 00:00:36.433
and corporate special interests
who are just fine,

00:00:36.444 --> 00:00:40.413
who are just fine with the way
things are going right now.

00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:44.413
They threw money, attack ads,
and outright lies at us every day for months.

00:00:44.424 --> 00:00:46.523
But we beat them anyway, didn't we?

00:00:50.724 --> 00:00:53.853
We were never the big money campaign.

00:00:53.864 --> 00:00:59.633
We're the people-powered campaign,
a campaign of 200,000 individual donors

00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:01.662
and not a dime from corporate PACs.

00:01:02.903 --> 00:01:07.632
And we showed what happens when we stick
together, stand up for what's right, and never

00:01:07.643 --> 00:01:09.792
lose hope even when the odds are long.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:14.192
It was 579 days ago that we gathered
in this very room,

00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:18.272
a place where we celebrated many victories
with more to come tonight.

00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:23.432
And a place that has taught me everything
about serving the community that I know

00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:26.432
and love that has given me so many
opportunities in my life.

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:29.412
Nearly 20 months ago,
I said I knew we were living

00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:30.712
in deeply uncertain times.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:34.492
But I knew something else that Granite Staters
don't flinch.

00:01:34.503 --> 00:01:37.292
We don't give in.
We stand up and fight.

00:01:37.303 --> 00:01:39.462
And that's exactly what we did in this campaign.

00:01:41.763 --> 00:01:45.192
The fight we started in this room
and took to every corner

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:49.092
of New Hampshire is now headed
to Washington to get our state

00:01:49.103 --> 00:01:51.322
and our country on the right track
for the future.

00:01:53.663 --> 00:02:01.012
And so, and so I'll end tonight by saying this,
I am so grateful for everyone in this room

00:02:01.023 --> 00:02:02.932
and beyond who made this win possible.

00:02:02.943 --> 00:02:06.552
I want to thank my extended family
who has always shown up

00:02:06.563 --> 00:02:09.972
for me each and every day,
to my amazing parents who have

00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:15.932
set the best example of public service
and hard work and given back to

00:02:15.943 --> 00:02:17.701
the community and unconditional love.

00:02:19.142 --> 00:02:21.701
I want to thank the guy next to me,
my amazing husband van.

00:02:30.642 --> 00:02:31.661
How about this?

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.661
All right,
the wrong person was on the ballot apparently.

00:02:46.242 --> 00:02:48.111
But he's always been by my side.

00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:51.811
And look, tonight, win, lose or draw,
I'm the luckiest guy because I'm married

00:02:51.822 --> 00:02:53.161
to a man that I love.

00:02:57.502 --> 00:03:01.631
And despite all the negative attacks
and the lies,

00:03:01.642 --> 00:03:05.141
it's nice to know that love
and truth prevailed tonight.

00:03:07.962 --> 00:03:16.791
I want to thank my amazing campaign staff led
by our campaign manager Rachel Petrie who ran

00:03:16.802 --> 00:03:19.380
the most effective campaign our state has seen.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.910
I want to thank Beth Cunoff
and all the organizers at Organizing

00:03:24.921 --> 00:03:28.220
for New Hampshire for the work you did
to get out the vote.

00:03:30.101 --> 00:03:32.810
You worked hard
over the past year communicating

00:03:32.821 --> 00:03:35.450
with voters on the issues
that matter and you got it done.

00:03:35.461 --> 00:03:39.770
I want to thank our friends
in organized labor as well who stood

00:03:39.781 --> 00:03:44.490
shoulder to shoulder with us in this campaign,
and I can't wait to continue to work

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:49.010
with all of you to build a fairer future
for everyone who calls new hampshire home

00:03:49.021 --> 00:03:52.730
thank you to all the volunteers the folks
who chipped in who knocked

00:03:52.741 --> 00:03:57.590
on doors who made phone calls who got
voters rides to the polls who talked to

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.090
your friends and neighbors about the stakes.

00:03:59.101 --> 00:04:01.770
I wouldn't be standing
before you giving this speech tonight

00:04:01.781 --> 00:04:05.230
if it weren't for the thousands
of folks who have stepped up

00:04:05.241 --> 00:04:05.890
for this campaign.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:10.900
Thanks for being a part of this.
And I want to thank the

00:04:10.921 --> 00:04:14.580
team in my congressional office too,
led by Steven Carlson and Carrie Thurman.

00:04:20.041 --> 00:04:25.529
They've spent the past eight years stepping up
for granted staters and meeting the needs

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.589
of our constituents in the entire district.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.899
And I just salute them for all their hard work
on behalf of New Hampshire.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.509
I want to thank my friend
of the New Hampshire delegation,

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.259
the amazing Senator Maggie Hassan
for joining us here tonight.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.869
It's going to be an honor to be
with her as part of the team

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.889
in the United States Senate,
working closely together

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.089
for the people of this state.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.829
And I want to send my best wishes to
my friend Maggie Goodlander

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:52.919
on her victory tonight.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.929
And my friend,
who I think you'll be hearing from shortly,

00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.939
Stephanie Shaheen.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.669
Look before I close,
I just want to recognize someone who is

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.409
important to all of us here
in this room and who has made an immeasurable

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.689
difference for the people of New Hampshire
throughout her time in public service,

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:29.518
and that's the great Senator Jeanne Jeanne, c'est que je vous, c'est que je
vous

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:37.328
Senator Shaheen has set the standard
we should all strive for in public service,

00:05:37.339 --> 00:05:40.428
and I couldn't be more grateful to call
her a colleague and a friend.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:43.968
We know that New Hampshire is a better place
because of the work she's done

00:05:43.979 --> 00:05:47.768
throughout her career and her impact
on education, on health care,

00:05:47.779 --> 00:05:51.128
on the environment, the economy,
and so many other crucial issues

00:05:51.139 --> 00:05:52.868
will stand the test of time.

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:53.808
So know this.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:57.288
No one will ever fill her shoes
but we all have got to carry

00:05:57.299 --> 00:06:04.428
on her good work don't we so tonight
we celebrate and as we celebrate let's think

00:06:04.439 --> 00:06:07.808
about the brighter future
that we can all build together let's

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:12.068
remember what is possible when we join
with common purpose and fight for a fairer,

00:06:12.079 --> 00:06:12.808
freer New Hampshire.

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:15.468
Today, you all did your part.

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:18.768
We all did our part to put our state
and our country on a better path.

00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:21.268
And tomorrow,
we've got to get to work to fight

00:06:21.279 --> 00:06:23.707
for what's right
and deliver the solutions that are

00:06:23.718 --> 00:06:24.627
desperately needed.

00:06:24.638 --> 00:06:30.307
So my words to you tonight are thank you,
and let's keep going.

00:06:30.318 --> 00:06:31.437
Let's keep going.

00:06:32.998 --> 00:06:36.487
Let's keep going and fighting and working
for the people of this great state.

00:06:36.498 --> 00:06:39.307
Thank you all for being here tonight.
I really appreciate it.

00:06:39.318 --> 00:06:40.737
Thanks for standing with us.

